 and both teams  demonstrated yes now some of the things  that we did and did not see  what we did see a lot of was games were  won or lost by player communication it  was the wall from the garage to the  waiter the attacking team was constantly  talking it's like Counter Strike they  had names for all the rooms and when  somebody went down they would like talk  to each other about what room something  happened in like oh guy went down in the  bedroom and so they'd be telling each  other that same with the defending team  just it seemed like map memorization and  communication was the biggest part of  these of winning or losing these rounds  yeah this is one of those games that'll  take a while to you know a good you know  week after it drops to like get familiar  with all the environments before being  able to get to that level of  communication so a question that we also  had was you know the start of around why  didn't say it the defending team just  blow out all the walls and kill the  attacking team on their way in or like  why didn't the attacking team to shoot  up the whole house and just whatever  happens happens so we looked at the ammo  counts it turns out that on both sides  ammo was very limited in this build so  each each class had about 60 rounds of  ammunition that really only broke down  into two clips and you can burn through  two clips very very quickly in a  firefight anybody who's played a shooter  knows that  so speaking of shooters Ryan how do you  feel about this game overall so far I'm  optimistic going in I was a big fan of  Search and Destroy in Call of Duty and  also diffuse in battlefield so that kind  of single spawn tactical communication  based gameplay is I'm a fan of that and  I'm really excited for you know I've  said this over and over again when we've  been covering other shooters but I'm  really excited for a game that feels  like it's actually pushing technical  boundaries and for me the Destruction is  doing that the the ability to like  grapple anymore on the house and come  through any window or come through the  floor you know maybe even the ceiling I  think that's what gives these games  immense replayability is just trusting  players to do things that are  unpredictable  so Rainbow six siege is coming out in  2015 on ps4 Xbox one and PC stay tuned  to games but comm for more Rainbow six  siege coverage  you
 

